##
## Multiphase (core-shell) condensate demo parameter file.
##
## Four sticky 5-bead species A, B, C, D that arrange into four CONCENTRIC layers:
## A in the core, then B, C and D as successive shells.
##
## The layering is engineered through the interaction matrix:
##
##   * Every species attracts ITSELF equally strongly (all self terms -25), so all
##     four condense into one droplet.
##   * IMMEDIATE NEIGHBOURS in the stack attract each other (A-B, B-C, C-D = -20),
##     so consecutive layers wet one another and stay in contact.
##   * NON-NEIGHBOURS REPEL (A-C, A-D, B-D = +15), so a layer refuses to touch any
##     layer other than the two it is meant to sit between. That repulsion is what
##     forces the four species into a nested A|B|C|D onion rather than a blob.
##
## (Which species ends up in the core is set by the seed - see build_onion_seed.py.
## With these symmetric interactions the seeded A|B|C|D order is a stable minimum.)
##
## Bead types:  A = core,  B, C = middle shells,  D = outer shell
##

## ANGLE PENALTIES (fully flexible chains)
ANGLE_PENALTY	A	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	B	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	C	0	0	0
ANGLE_PENALTY	D	0	0	0

## PAIRWISE SHORT-RANGE INTERACTIONS (negative = attractive, positive = repulsive)
##            self   adjacent   non-adjacent
A	A	-25
A	B	-20
A	C	15
A	D	15
B	B	-25
B	C	-20
B	D	15
C	C	-25
C	D	-20
D	D	-25

## bead-solvent interactions (all zero: the only driving forces are the pair terms)
A	0	0
B	0	0
C	0	0
D	0	0
